# Lexicon

The tells the scan looks for, to read a text against by hand when `scripts/scan.sh` can't run. Patterns are Go regular expressions; `(?i)` means case-insensitive and `\x{2192}` names a character by code point.

## Tier 1

A match is a hit to rewrite.

- `hope-helps`: `(?i)\bI hope (this|that) helps\b` -> cut it

## Tier 2

A match is a hit to rewrite.

- `arrow`: `\x{2192}` (on commit, pr) -> use ASCII

## Tier 3

A match counts toward density only.

- `ui-glass`: `backdrop-blur` (on ui)

## Density

A text is dense at 3 or more tier 3 matches and 3 or more per 100 words of prose. These words count:

delve, align with
